<!-- SECTION: MEANING -->
<section class="content4 cid-meaning" id="meaning">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-lg-8 text-center">
        <h2 class="display-2"><strong>What Is Yom Teruah?</strong></h2>
        <p class="display-7 mt-3">
          Yom Teruah is the appointed time of HaShem marking the beginning of the seventh month. 
          It is a day of sounding the shofar, gathering together, and remembering His covenant. 
          Scripture gives no additional traditions — only the command to rest, assemble, and hear the Teruah.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
